# ============================================================
# File:        .dockerignore  (REPOSITORY ROOT)
# Project:     RaceArena — IMAGE-STANDALONE-1
#
# THE BUILD CONTEXT IS THE REPOSITORY ROOT, so this file — and only this file — decides what is sent
# to the Docker daemon. `.dockerignore` is honoured at the CONTEXT ROOT and nowhere else.
#
# ── WHY THIS FILE HAD TO EXIST BEFORE THE CONTEXT MOVED ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# It is written first, deliberately, because moving the context is the kind of change that silently
# undoes a protection that has nothing to do with it.
#
# The credential exclusion used to live in `server/.dockerignore`. That worked because `./server` WAS
# the context root. The moment the context becomes the repository root, that file stops being
# honoured at all — and the build context becomes the entire tree. Measured, not feared:
#
#     context = ./server, its own ignore honoured        94 files      55.1 MB
#     context = repository root, NO ignore file       30,502 files   ~1,306 MB
#     context = repository root, THIS file            (see below)
#
# That 1.3 GB includes `client/node_modules`, `reports/` and — the part that matters —
# `server/data/`, which holds `users.json`, `users.json.bak-*`, `sessions.sqlite` and
# `setup-complete.json`. IMAGE-NO-CREDENTIALS-1 removed those from the image on 2026-09-01; without
# this file they would have walked straight back in, through a change about `shared/`.
#
# `server/.dockerignore` is DELETED rather than left in place. An ignore file that is honoured or not
# depending on which context someone builds from is two sources of truth for one fact, and this
# repository has paid for that shape repeatedly. Its reasoning lives here now.
#
# ── WHY DENY-BY-DEFAULT ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This is an ALLOW-LIST: everything is excluded, then exactly what the image needs is re-included.
# A deny-list would need a new line every time a file worth protecting is added, and the failure
# mode of forgetting one is that a secret ships. Deny-by-default is the same principle the auth layer
# uses, for the same reason: the cost of an omission should be a broken build, not a leak.
#
# TO ADD SOMETHING TO THE IMAGE: add a `!` line below AND a COPY in server/Dockerfile. If you add
# only the COPY, the build fails loudly on a missing path — which is the direction you want.
# ============================================================

# Everything, by default.
**

# ── What the server image actually needs, and nothing else ───────────────────────────────────────

# Its dependency manifest. `npm install --omit=dev` runs against this.
!server/package.json

# The server itself.
!server/src/**
!server/utils/**

# ── …BUT NOT ITS TESTS (IMAGE-NO-TESTS-1) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The two lines above take the directories WHOLE, and this repository keeps a test beside the file it
# tests — `racers.test.js` sits next to `racers.js`. So 31 test files rode into every image: MEASURED
# in the running container as 62 files under /app/src + /app/utils, of which 31 were `*.test.js`,
# 354,556 bytes. HALF the server source a recipient receives was tests that cannot run there and that
# describe the system's internals to somebody who only wants to play the game.
#
# THE RULE LIVES HERE AND NOT IN THE DOCKERFILE, deliberately. This file is the one place that
# decides what the image contains; a `RUN find … -delete` in the Dockerfile would be a second such
# place, and the two would drift the way every second home in this repository has. It also keeps the
# files out of the CONTEXT rather than deleting them from a layer they already entered.
#
# THE SET WAS ESTABLISHED BY SHAPE, NOT BY ONE SUFFIX, and the sweep found more than was reported:
# 29 under `server/src/` and TWO MORE under `server/utils/` (`imageUpload.test.js`,
# `isSafeAssetFilename.test.js`). There are no `.spec.` files and no `__tests__` directory anywhere
# under `server/`, and no test-only fixture or helper hides among the source: all 31 NON-test files
# in these two directories were resolved by import specifier and every one has a production consumer.
# Nothing in the image imports a test file, so nothing here can break by their absence — which was
# then proved by booting the image with no source mounts at all.
server/src/**/*.test.js
server/utils/**/*.test.js

# The shipped seed records. These are how a fresh install gets its ten tracks and their backgrounds
# (proven by booting an image against an empty volume), so they are load-bearing and must be here.
!server/seeds/**

# THE ONLY THING THE SERVER IMPORTS FROM OUTSIDE `server/`, and the reason the context moved at all.
# Established by resolving every relative specifier in `server/src` and `server/utils` against its
# importing file — 65 of them — rather than by copying the directory because it looked relevant:
# `server/src/routes/playerGroups.js` imports `../../../shared/nameLimits.mjs`, which from
# `/app/src/routes/` resolves to `/shared/`. That is the whole list; `shared/` contains this one file.
!shared/nameLimits.mjs

# ── Deliberately NOT re-included, named so the absences are decisions rather than oversights ─────
#
#   server/data/**    THE RUNTIME STORE. Accounts, sessions and the setup marker live there beside
#                     the seeded records. An operator's data belongs in a volume, never in a layer.
#                     This is the exclusion IMAGE-NO-CREDENTIALS-1 built, carried across intact.
#   server/test/**    Test harness. Not run in the image.
#   *.test.js         THE TESTS THAT LIVE BESIDE THE SOURCE, re-excluded above after `server/src/**`
#                     and `server/utils/**` admit their directories whole (IMAGE-NO-TESTS-1). 31
#                     files, measured in the running container, and they cannot run in the image:
#                     `vitest` is a devDependency and `npm install --omit=dev` never installs it.
#                     What they cost is not bytes — 0.64% of the context — it is that they hand a
#                     recipient a description of the internals with the game.
#   server/scripts/** `dev-start.js` and `restart-dev.js`, the local dev-loop wrappers. Already
#                     excluded because nothing re-includes them; named here so that is a decision
#                     and not an accident. The image's CMD is `node src/index.js` directly.
#   client/**         The built client arrives through a NAMED BUILD CONTEXT
#                     (`additional_contexts: { client: ./client }`), which is a separate context and
#                     is not filtered by this file. The client SOURCE has no business in the image.
#   scripts/, docs/, reports/, .git/, node_modules/   None of it runs in the container.
